# Google Calendar Integration — OAuth 2.0 Setup
# ============================================
#
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com
# 2. Create a new project (or select existing), name it "MindFlow"
# 3. Enable the Google Calendar API:
#    APIs & Services → Library → search "Google Calendar API" → Enable
# 4. Configure OAuth consent screen:
#    APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#    - User Type: External
#    - App name: MindFlow
#    - User support email: your email
#    - Developer contact: your email
#    - Scopes: Add calendar.readonly and calendar.events
#    - Test users: Add your email address
# 5. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID:
#    APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth client ID
#    - Application type: Web application
#    - Name: MindFlow Web Client
#    - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        http://localhost:5173
#        https://mindflow-liart.vercel.app
#        Add EVERY deployed frontend domain here — e.g. the Netlify
#        domain if you deploy there. A missing origin fails OAuth with
#        "origin_mismatch" at sign-in time.
#    - No redirect URIs needed (uses implicit flow via GIS)
# 6. Copy your Client ID below:
#
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Backend API origin — OPTIONAL. The app runs fully client-side by
# default; src/utils/api.js falls back to this exact URL in production
# builds, so this only needs setting if the Render service moves.
# VITE_API_ORIGIN=https://mindflow-api.onrender.com
